# The ALSA test reaches its server through alsa-lib's pulse plugin,
# which runs libpulse's threaded main loop on a thread of its own
# (pa_thread_new). libpulse and libpulsecommon are not instrumented,
# so ThreadSanitizer misreads their locking (a pthread_cond_wait it
# sees as an unlock of an unlocked mutex) and their free lists. Only
# calls made from inside those libraries are suppressed; the library's
# own code is not.
called_from_lib:libpulse.so
called_from_lib:libpulsecommon
